      "claim": "Adult gray whales are 13–15 m long, about 3.5 m tall at the highest point of the body, and weigh 30–40 t.",
      "evidence": "NOAA and marine‑mammal fact sheets for Eschrichtius robustus list average adult length ≈13–15 m, maximum body height ≈3–4 m, and mass ≈30–40 tons.",
